# ── Sarapis workspace root ignore ──────────────────────────────────────────
# site/ and design-system/ ship their own .gitignore (node_modules, .next,
# dist, media, chromium cache, .env). This closes the remaining root-level gaps.

# OS
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# Secrets / env (belt-and-suspenders — subdir gitignores also cover site/.env).
# Example files are kept.
.env
*.env
!*.env.example

# Claude Code — personal/local settings (launch.json is tracked)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Runtime data — the SQLite content DB + backups + WAL/SHM. Regenerable / lives
# on the box; not source. (Keep the code, not the data.)
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.bak-*

# Deploy artifacts — the cross-built image tarballs are hundreds of MB.
*.tar.gz
site/deploy/*.tar.gz

# Migration inputs/outputs — the WordPress export + derived JSON (re-exportable
# from WP / regenerable via migration/extract_wxr.py).
sarapis.WordPress.*.xml
migration/out/

# Node (safety net in case a stray package lands outside the subdir ignores)
**/node_modules/

# Logs
*.log

# ── Kept OUT of the public repo (they stay on disk for maintainers) ─────────
# Operational detail: hosts, deploy targets, credential locations, incident
# history. Claude Code loads CLAUDE.local.md automatically after CLAUDE.md.
CLAUDE.local.md
CLAUDE.local.archive.md
CONTINUE.md
# Code reviews may describe unfixed vulnerabilities.
REVIEW-*.md
# One-shot scripts and runbooks written for a specific production box.
site/deploy/DEPLOY-round37-multibrand.md
site/deploy/curate-feed-r4*.py
site/deploy/migrate-repo-rename.py
# Design-tool deliverables and a bundled prototype — working files, not source.
handoff/
Sarapis Activity.html
remote_site/
# TypeScript incremental build cache.
*.tsbuildinfo

# Python bytecode (the backup tests generate it)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
